<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Glory to Hong Kong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">26 August <a href="/years/2019">2019</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · <a href="/today-in-history/august-26">On this day: 26 August</a> · Also known as 願榮光歸香港, Jyun wing gwong gwai Hoeng Gong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Glory to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a>&quot; is a protest anthem of the 2019–2020 Hong Kong protests. Since mass protests against the extradition bill broke out in early June 2019, demonstrators had sung songs such as &quot;Do You Hear the People Sing?&quot; from Les Misérables and &quot;Sing Hallelujah to the Lord&quot;.</p></div>
